# reclogin's PAM service on AcornOS, installed as /etc/pam.d/reclogin.
#
# Alpine's layout: the same four base files as linux-pam's own `login`
# service (the one util-linux-login and shadow-login use). base-session
# is expected to carry `-session optional pam_elogind.so`, which registers
# the session with elogind from the XDG_SEAT, XDG_VTNR, XDG_SESSION_TYPE,
# XDG_SESSION_CLASS and XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP that reclogind puts into the
# PAM environment. base-auth and base-session also carry the desktop
# wallets' optional modules.
#
# pam_elogind is listed once more after base-session, so that the session is
# registered even where base-session does not carry it. Where it does, the
# second call does nothing: pam_elogind leaves a process that is already in
# a session alone.
auth      include    base-auth
account   include    base-account
password  include    base-password
session   include    base-session
-session  optional   pam_elogind.so
